+/*
+ * A button whose pin can raise an interrupt reports a change the moment its
+ * edge arrives instead of on the next poll (up to poll-interval later). After
+ * any edge it settles: further edges are ignored and the pin is read again
+ * when GHAZAL_BUTTON_SETTLE_MS have passed, so contact bounce cannot report
+ * extra presses, and a change during the settling time (a release, or an
+ * edge lost while the pin was briefly muxed as an input to be read) is
+ * reported then.
+ */
+#define GHAZAL_BUTTON_SETTLE_MS	5
+
